title: HaroldAudenClue0
---
Harold Auden’s grandfather lived on a few acres of land out in the countryside. Poorly maintained, the grass would grow tall, nearly the size of an 8 year-old Harold. On a visit during the peak of summer, Harold escape his mother’s eye and ran out in the vast field. He pretended to be a lion, on the hunt for its prey. The fantasy died quickly as the mother yelled his name and Harold was forced to come sulking back. After an expected finger wagging, his mother began inspecting his body. A blood-curdling scream filled Harold’s consciousness as his mother jumped back at the sight of a tick feasting on the young boys leg. After removal, the next week was a slew of doctor’s visits, of which nothing ever came.
===

title: HaroldAudenClue1
---
While Harold was fascinated by horror stories growing up, nothing stuck with him quite like the story of the Dunwich Horror. A being somewhere between human and cosmic god, the idea of a human-figure hiding evil beneath the skin disturbed him. He could feel bugs running under his skin whenever he thought about it. He would stay awake at night imagining a human face melting across a humongous pile of flesh and tentacles, the Dunwich Horror in its true form.
===

title: HaroldAudenClue2
---
Harold’s school life was a sad but familiar story. His overbearing mother left him with crippling fear at the thought of interacting with other students. He had one friend growing up named Jacob Allerton. A similarly shy boy, Jacob and Harold didn’t talk much. They would simply sit together during class and occasionally exchange glances. One day, Harold’s mother took the liberty of inviting Jacob over for a playdate. Suffice to say, the friendship ended with Harold’s blood washing away sidewalk chalk and Jacob being unceremoniously moved to another school, towns away.
===
